        "question": "Why do so many campus relationships break up during ASUU strikes?",
        "answer": "Strike breakups occur because couples accustomed to constant campus proximity struggle with the sudden shift to long-distance communication. Without shared lectures and daily routines, unresolved insecurities, lack of scheduled check-ins, and hometown distractions cause relationships to drift apart. Establishing regular communication routines and offering mutual encouragement during uncertain shutdowns keeps relationships resilient, grounded, and emotionally vibrant."
